# NOTES #

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-18]  The final version of " [LINK: (Song for Bob Dylan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_for_Bob_Dylan] " was also recorded on this day. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTECann2010224-17]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-22]  Wakeman had played previously  [LINK: (Mellotron) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mellotron]  on Bowie's  [LINK: (1969 self-titled album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Bowie_(1969_album)] . [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTECann2010155-21]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-24]  Wakeman played the same 1898  [LINK: (Bechstein) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C._Bechstein]  piano that was used by  [LINK: (the Beatles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles]  for " [LINK: (Hey Jude) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hey_Jude] " (1968), and later by  [LINK: (Queen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_(band)]  for " [LINK: (Bohemian Rhapsody) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bohemian_Rhapsody] " (1975). [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPegg2016347-23]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-39]  See sources for specific attribution: Doggett and O'Leary made comparisons to the  [LINK: (timpani) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timpani]  from the "main theme" of 2001, [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEO'Leary2015chap._5-4]  [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDoggett2012150-30]  while Pegg and Sandford compared it to Also sprach Zarathustra. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPegg2016162–163-13]  [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTESandford199785-37]  According to David Cheal of the  [LINK: (Financial Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Times] , Also sprach Zarathustra was used as the main theme for 2001. [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-38]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-53]  Some sources give the release date as 17 November 1971 in the UK and 4 December in the US. [LINK: ([45]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPegg2016343–350-49]  [LINK: ([46]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTECann2010230–234-50]  [LINK: ([47]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEClerc2021117:_US_date-51]  According to the biographer Chris O'Leary, the US date was before the UK one, although he questions Billboard's reported date of Saturday, 4 December. He does, however, clarify the UK date as 17 December. [LINK: ([48]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEO'Leary2015Notes_on_chap._5-52]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-63]  Laroche was Bowie's make-up artist for the covers of  [LINK: (Aladdin Sane) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aladdin_Sane]  and  [LINK: (Pin Ups) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pin_Ups]  (both 1973), as well as the 1973 leg of the  [LINK: (Ziggy Stardust Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziggy_Stardust_Tour] . [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPegg2016363-61]  Burretti was an openly gay dress designer whom Bowie chose as the frontman for the band Arnold Corns in early 1971. [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTECann2010207-62]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_ref-142]  Nine Inch Nails were the opening act during Bowie's 1995  [LINK: (Outside Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outside_Tour] . Two years later, Reznor created several remixes of Bowie's track " [LINK: (I'm Afraid of Americans) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I%27m_Afraid_of_Americans] " and appeared in the song's music video. [LINK: ([134]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBuckley2005438,_453-140]  [LINK: ([135]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPegg2016128–129-141]


